From 55ace56ee4ab1b245c57f540c846726d869b6b3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Louvignes <olivier@mgcrea.io>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:00:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/55] drm/ingenic: add a driver for the X1600 LCD controller

The X1600 LCD controller has none of the registers ingenic-drm programs: it
fetches each frame through a descriptor whose address it takes from FRM_DESC,
and keeps its interface, TFT timings and smart panel set-up in separate
register blocks. This driver handles parallel RGB panels on a 24-bit bus,
with one full-screen plane in RGB565 or XRGB8888. Each descriptor points at
itself, so a frame repeats until a flip links the next descriptor in, which
the controller follows at the end of the frame.

The register layout comes from the vendor kernel's driver, as rewritten under
the GPL for HiBy's players.
